anthra skins for text2skin on Debian
====================================

The anthra skins by Tomas Saxer are generated from XML parts according to a
set of options. Each skin package installs

  /usr/share/vdr-skin-anthra/SKIN   the skin sources (read-only)
  /etc/vdr/anthra/SKIN.conf         the options (conffile)

and builds the skin into /var/lib/vdr/plugins/text2skin/SKIN on
installation and upgrade.

To change the skin, edit /etc/vdr/anthra/SKIN.conf, then run

  vdr-skin-anthra-update SKIN

and restart VDR. Your options are kept on upgrades, dpkg asks if the
default options of a new package version differ from yours.

Channel logos, separator logos and EPG images are not part of the
packages, set their paths in the options (slashes escaped with
backslashes). Logos for the anthra skins: http://www.anthra.de/anthra-skins/

 -- Frank Neumann <fnu@vdr-portal.de>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200
